# Copy to $HARNESS_INSTANCE_DIR/harness.env (default instance/harness.env) and edit.
# Sourced by bin/tick.sh, so it is shell: quote values with spaces. HARNESS_INSTANCE_DIR and
# HARNESS_ENV are read from the environment only, never from this file.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The checkout ticks start in; they never edit it, only create worktrees from it.
TARGET_REPO=/path/to/checkout
# Where ticks create their worktrees, outside the checkout so they never show in its status.
WORKTREE_ROOT=/path/to/worktrees

# --- GitHub -----------------------------------------------------------------
# owner/name ([HOST/]OWNER/NAME off github.com); empty derives it from TARGET_REPO's origin remote,
# and `tick.sh check` fails when that remote names none.
GH_REPO=
# A token for gh when cron has no gh login; the cron scripts and the dashboard pass it to gh only.
# GH_TOKEN=
# Only issues carrying it are ever worked.
ISSUE_LABEL=ai
# Marks an issue a tick has claimed.
WIP_LABEL=ai:wip
# Marks an issue whose verified PR waits for the merge slot.
READY_LABEL=ai:ready
# Parks an issue until the owner signs it off; no tick claims it.
SIGNOFF_LABEL=ai:signoff
# Parks an issue until an operator answers it; no tick claims it.
OPERATOR_LABEL=ai:operator
# The GitHub logins whose `Operator` comments bind a tick and wake the supervisor, space-separated;
# unset, the repository's owner, members and collaborators.
# OPERATOR_LOGINS="owner-a"
# Takes an issue before any older fresh one.
FIRST_LABEL=ai:first
# Counts an issue only when nothing else is claimable.
LOW_LABEL=ai:low
# Gives an issue the long tick budget; only the operator sets it.
LONG_LABEL=ai:long
# Prefix of the branches ticks create, so pr-sweep.sh touches only the harness's own.
BRANCH_PREFIX=ai/
# The branch ticks merge into; empty skips keeping a base tree for it in worktree-gc.sh.
WORK_BRANCH=
# Worktree directory names worktree-gc.sh never removes, space-separated.
WORKTREE_KEEP=
# Seconds hooks/worktree-busy may take; past it, or on its failure, worktree-gc.sh removes nothing.
# WORKTREE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_S=30
# A base tree stays while its commit was WORK_BRANCH's head in the last KEEP_HOURS or is one of
# its last KEEP_HEADS heads: a long run can read it for hours after the branch moved.
# KEEP_HOURS=6
# KEEP_HEADS=3

# --- pool sizing ------------------------------------------------------------
# The harness binary (cargo build --release --bin harness); the default is the checkout's
# target/release/harness, else harness on PATH. Set it above any key that names it.
# HARNESS_BIN=/path/to/harness
# A project-aware queue count (`harness claimable` honours Depends on: and the labels above). A command
# line split on whitespace without quoting, so no path in it may contain a space.
QUEUE_DEPTH_CMD="$HARNESS_BIN claimable"
# Upper bound on concurrent ticks; the agents' usage windows lower it (harness usage).
MAX_SLOTS=4
# Width the usage steps scale from, when it should differ from MAX_SLOTS.
# TICK_WIDTH=4
# Seconds between spawning runners, so parallel ticks do not claim the same issue.
STAGGER_SECONDS=8
# Minimum seconds between heartbeat ticks while the queue is empty.
HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL=1800
# A tick shorter than this found nothing or failed, so its runner stops chaining.
CHAIN_MIN_TICK_S=180
# Most ticks one runner chains before it hands back to cron.
MAX_CHAIN=24
# A tick younger than this counts as about to claim a queued issue.
CLAIM_GRACE_S=360

# --- ticks ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One priority list across agents, best first: agent:model, agent@account:model for a tick on one
# of the agent's accounts (below), or a model TICK_AGENT runs. An entry
# whose agent hit its usage limit is skipped for MODEL_COOLDOWN_S, and one whose agent's windows
# allow no more ticks is passed over, so the next entry, maybe another vendor's, runs.
# For example: TICK_MODELS="claude:claude-opus-5-5 codex:gpt-5.5 gemini:gemini-3-pro"
TICK_MODELS=claude:claude-opus-5-5
# The agent of an entry that names none.
TICK_AGENT=claude
# Seconds an entry that hit its usage limit is skipped.
MODEL_COOLDOWN_S=1800
# A separate entry (agent:model or agent@account:model) for issues labelled LANE_LABEL; both empty
# turn the lane off.
LANE_MODEL=
LANE_LABEL=
# Minutes from claim to summary, stated in every claim.
TICK_BUDGET_MIN=60
# Minutes for an issue carrying LONG_LABEL.
LONG_TICK_BUDGET_MIN=120
# More names from this file exported to each tick, for the installation's prompt to use. The paths,
# GH_REPO, the labels and the PUBLIC_RECORD_* keys always are; GH_TOKEN and GITHUB_TOKEN never are.
TICK_EXPORTS=""
# Seconds hooks/hold may take before the harness treats it as not held.
HOLD_TIMEOUT_S=5

# --- accounts (docs/INSTANCE.md) --------------------------------------------
# Several accounts of one agent CLI, each a folder signed in to once by hand:
# <root>/claude/claude-<name> (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR), <root>/codex/codex-<name> (CODEX_HOME),
# <root>/gemini/gemini-<name> (GEMINI_CLI_HOME); a name is 1 to 32 of a-z, 0-9 and -. Unset, accounts
# are off. Read the providers' terms first: several accounts for separate purposes (work, personal,
# a client) are the safe use, not one queue spread across accounts for more usage. An absolute path,
# with $HOME rather than ~; each folder must be writable by its owner only (chmod go-w), and an
# account signs in only through its folder, never the agent's API key variables.
# AGENT_ACCOUNTS_DIR=$HOME/.agents-accounts
# For example: TICK_MODELS="claude@work:claude-opus-5-5 claude@client-a:claude-opus-5-5 codex@work:gpt-5.5"
# Each account reads its own folder's usage, never USAGE_SOURCE_<agent> or USAGE_FETCH_<agent>; these
# replace one account's, a - of its name written _.
# A claude account runs only its own fetch, which must read that account's login (docs/INSTANCE.md):
# without one it starts no tick, since USAGE_FETCH would read the default account's.
# USAGE_FETCH_claude_client_a=/path/to/client-a-usage-fetch
# USAGE_SOURCE_claude_client_a=json:/path/to/client-a-usage.json

# --- supervisor (docs/INSTANCE.md) ------------------------------------------
# 1 runs a supervisor tick on events and honours its directive; empty, neither happens.
SUPERVISOR=
# Its agent:model (or agent@account:model), on this host, claude or codex; the last TICK_MODELS
# entry unless set.
# SUPERVISOR_MODEL=claude:claude-opus-5-5
# The flags that run it with no tools, replacing the defaults docs/INSTANCE.md gives.
# SUPERVISOR_FLAGS_claude="--tools= --restricted --strict-mcp-config --disable-slash-commands --no-session-persistence"
# Minutes it may run.
# SUPERVISOR_BUDGET_MIN=10
# It runs at least this often, and never sooner than the minimum after its last start.
# SUPERVISOR_INTERVAL_S=1800
# SUPERVISOR_MIN_INTERVAL_S=600
# The longest a directive lasts.
# SUPERVISOR_MAX_DIRECTIVE_S=21600
# How long a tick it stops has to wind down.
# SUPERVISOR_STOP_GRACE_S=1200
# The most issues it parks for the operator in 24 hours.
# SUPERVISOR_MAX_PARKS_PER_DAY=2

# --- usage windows (docs/INSTANCE.md) ---------------------------------------
# Where each agent's windows come from: json:<path>, claude-cache:<path>, codex-sessions[:<dir>] or
# none. Missing or stale, the agent starts nothing; none leaves only the usage-limit cooldown.
# USAGE_SOURCE_claude=claude-cache:$HOME/.claude/usage-cache.json
# USAGE_SOURCE_codex=codex-sessions:$HOME/.codex/sessions
# Every other agent must name its source: gemini keeps no usage reading, so only its usage-limit
# cooldown gates it.
USAGE_SOURCE_gemini=none
# Claude's cache, and the script that refreshes it (USAGE_FETCH_<agent> for any agent's source).
USAGE_CACHE=$HOME/.claude/usage-cache.json
USAGE_FETCH=$HOME/.claude/scripts/usage-fetch.sh
# USAGE_FETCH_gemini=/path/to/gemini-usage-fetch
# A reading older than this is unknown.
USAGE_MAX_AGE=1800
# A reading younger than this is not refreshed.
USAGE_REFRESH_AFTER=120
# No window may reach it.
USAGE_CEILING_PCT=90
# Where a running tick stands down in a window under a day; two under the ceiling unless set.
# USAGE_TICK_STOP_PCT=88
# Where it stands down in a longer window; USAGE_TICK_STOP_PCT unless set.
# USAGE_TICK_STOP_LONG_PCT=88
# A window under a day halves the pool, keeps one tick, and starts none at these points.
USAGE_STEPS_SHORT="60 70 80"
# A longer window's same three points; it fills slower, so they sit higher.
USAGE_STEPS_LONG="80 85 88"
# One window's own points, by agent and window name.
# USAGE_STEPS_claude_weekly="80 85 88"

# --- agents -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Each local tick pipes its prompt to AGENT_BIN_<agent> (default: the agent's name) with
# AGENT_FLAGS_<agent>. Ticks are unattended and cannot answer permission prompts, so the defaults
# turn them off; set but empty passes no flag.
# AGENT_BIN_claude=claude
# AGENT_FLAGS_claude=--dangerously-skip-permissions
# AGENT_BIN_codex=codex
# AGENT_FLAGS_codex=--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox
# AGENT_BIN_gemini=gemini
# AGENT_FLAGS_gemini=--yolo
# The extended regex an agent's usage-limit message matches, when its CLI words it otherwise.
# AGENT_LIMIT_RE_codex="You've hit your usage limit|rate_limit_reached"

# --- fleet (docs/FLEET.md) --------------------------------------------------
# 1 runs each tick through `fleet dispatch`, with the entry's agent as the adapter, instead of a
# local agent CLI; AGENT_BIN_* and AGENT_FLAGS_* then do not apply, the device's fleetd.toml fixes
# the agent's command line.
FLEET_DISPATCH=
# The device a tick goes to; auto picks the least-loaded device with a free place for the agent.
FLEET_DEVICE=auto
# The fleet CLI, a name looked up on HARNESS_PATH or a path.
FLEET_BIN=fleet
# The device registry; $HARNESS_INSTANCE_DIR/fleet.toml unless set.
# FLEET_CONFIG=/path/to/fleet.toml
# Seconds `tick.sh check` waits for `fleet status --json`.
# FLEET_CHECK_TIMEOUT_S=60
# PATH for cron, which starts with almost none.
HARNESS_PATH=$HOME/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# Tick logs kept in $HARNESS_STATE/logs.
LOG_RETENTION=200
# Logs and locks; $HARNESS_HOME/state unless set.
# HARNESS_STATE=/path/to/state
# pr-sweep.sh's log; $HARNESS_STATE/logs/pr-sweep.log unless set.
# PR_SWEEP_LOG=/path/to/pr-sweep.log

# --- the public record ------------------------------------------------------
# Sections a PR body and an issue body must carry, comma-separated, matched as prefixes.
# PUBLIC_RECORD_PR_SECTIONS="Summary,Why,What changed,How to verify,Evidence,Scope and limits"
# PUBLIC_RECORD_ISSUE_SECTIONS="Summary,Ask"
# The installation's lint rules; $HARNESS_INSTANCE_DIR/lint_rules.json unless set.
# PUBLIC_RECORD_RULES=/path/to/lint_rules.json

# --- dashboard (every panel below is hidden while its keys are empty) -------
# Page title.
DASHBOARD_TITLE=
# Prints the shared-device status the resource panel shows, in the format docs/INSTANCE.md gives.
# The dashboard expands $HARNESS_HOME and $HARNESS_INSTANCE_DIR in this, DEVICE_PROBE_CMD and
# QUEUE_DEPTH_CMD, and nothing else.
RESOURCE_STATUS_CMD=
# Glob of run-queue directories, each with a status file.
RUN_QUEUE_GLOB=
# Process name that holds a run queue.
RUN_QUEUE_HOLDER=
# The queue log's file name in each run-queue directory; queue.log unless set.
RUN_QUEUE_LOG=
# Words in a queue's status that mean it stopped, space-separated.
RUN_QUEUE_STOP_WORDS=
# Split shell-style and run without a shell here; over ssh, as the same quoted words. Its first line
# is "<name>, <util %>, <memory used MiB>, <memory total MiB>", each further line a process on the
# device, "<pid>, <memory MiB>, <process name>" (nvidia-smi's csv,noheader,nounits form). A probe
# that needs pipes or several commands names its shell: sh -c '...'.
DEVICE_PROBE_CMD=
# Where the build locks live; /tmp unless set.
BUILD_LOCK_DIR=
# This host's build lock file name.
BUILD_LOCK_LOCAL=
# A remote host's build lock file name; {name} becomes the host's name below.
BUILD_LOCK_REMOTE=
# Each remote host's lock name, "<user@host>=<name> ...".
BUILD_LOCK_NAMES=
# Prints `fleet status --json`, read every 30 s for the Devices and Agent sessions panels. Split
# shell-style and run without a shell, like RESOURCE_STATUS_CMD.
FLEET_STATUS_CMD=
